{{// 🩹 Chibi DeepSeek patch, for DeepSeek V4, Pro and Flash. Native thinking stays one short pass through The Logic Core's lines, under 150 words with no rule audits, since DeepSeek otherwise thinks for a minute or two before every reply and writes worse the longer it thinks. u/BSPiotr caught it saying your words back to you and replaying the same fact or beat for several turns, and V4 Pro gave a character a tail her card never mentioned, so three lines go to the 🚪 Last-Mile Gate and into the plan (Echo, Repeats, Bodies, about 88 tokens). V4 Pro (0813) also writes in fragments, so a Joins line (about 47) joins every short sentence after a reply's first and folds a one-sentence paragraph into the one before it when the same voice carries on, while stalls, cut-offs and one-word answers stay. With 🔦 Flash Gate ON, as Flash users run it, Joins and the Flash Gate's Runs line both stay out, so Flash's prose stays as it was. With 🥰 Bonds Lite or 🎲 Fate & Chekhov Ledger ON, the plan also gets a Tally line (about 88 tokens with both): DeepSeek V4.1 Flash left Sparks, Grudge and BOND at their starting numbers turn after turn, so Tally has it write each pair's old numbers, name this turn's listed acts, slights and sincere repair, add Sparks (max 2, half while Grudge is 3 or more), add Grudge (a repair clears it), turn 7 Sparks into BOND +1 and 5 Grudge into BOND -1, and write the new numbers, then update the 🎲 ledger's q and hp counters and its last entry. The Tally line sits outside the thinking word cap, stays in the plan and out of the 🚪 Last-Mile Gate, and is absent while both modules are off and on an Impersonate turn; it relies on Bonds Lite's rule that strangers start at 0/0/0. DeepSeek V4 and V4.1 Flash users switch 🔦 Flash Gate ON too. Use one model patch at most.}}{{trim}}
{{#if .ariaBondsLine}}{{setvar::ariaPatchTally::- Tally: per pair, old BOND/Sparks/Grudge; this turn's listed acts, slights, sincere repair or none; Sparks +1/act (max 2, half at Grudge 3+), 7+: BOND +1, Sparks 0; Grudge +1/slight, repair clears it, 5+: BOND -1, Grudge 0; then the new three.}}{{#if .ariaFateLine}}{{setvar::ariaPatchTally::{{getvar::ariaPatchTally}} 🎲 q +1 on AMBIENT, else 0; hp = [hot] Bullets after this turn's changes, last = this turn's tier/source and happening.}}{{/if}}{{else}}{{#if .ariaFateLine}}{{setvar::ariaPatchTally::- Tally: 🎲 q +1 on AMBIENT, else 0; hp = [hot] Bullets after this turn's changes, last = this turn's tier/source and happening.}}{{/if}}{{/if}}Native reasoning: one pass of terse bullets per plan line under 150 words{{#if .ariaPatchTally}}, Tally aside{{/if}}; no drafts, rereads, audits or second passes, then write.{{setvar::ariaPatchLines::3}}{{setvar::ariaPatchGate::- Echo: confirm or answer {{user}}'s line by an act or own words, never by repeating it, single words too.
- Repeats: a told fact or description returns only when the story changes it; a played beat moves on.
- Bodies: if the card or first message describes a body, parts a plain human lacks, tails and wings included, appear only if named there, whatever the species; unnamed ones go unmentioned, hidden or absent alike.}}{{setvar::ariaPatchJoins::- Joins: past one a reply, a sentence under five words joins a neighbour, and a lone-sentence paragraph the one before if the same voice carries on; stalls, restarts, cut-off lines and one-word answers stay.}}

